## **Lesson 9: Conditional Logic (when/otherwise)**

Like IF-ELSE statements in SQL/Python!

---

### **1. Basic when/otherwise**

```python
from pyspark.sql.functions import when, col

data = [(1, "Alice", 25), (2, "Bob", 30), (3, "Charlie", 35)]
df = spark.createDataFrame(data, ["id", "name", "age"])

# Single condition
df.withColumn(
    "age_group",
    when(col("age") > 30, "Senior").otherwise("Junior")
).show()
```

**Output:**
```
+---+-------+---+---------+
| id|   name|age|age_group|
+---+-------+---+---------+
|  1|  Alice| 25|   Junior|
|  2|    Bob| 30|   Junior|
|  3|Charlie| 35|   Senior|
+---+-------+---+---------+
```

---

### **2. Multiple Conditions (IF-ELIF-ELSE)**

```python
df.withColumn(
    "category",
    when(col("age") < 25, "Young")
    .when(col("age") < 30, "Adult")
    .otherwise("Senior")
).show()
```

---

### **3. Conditions Based on Multiple Columns**

```python
data = [(1, "Alice", 80000, "Sales"), 
        (2, "Bob", 60000, "HR"),
        (3, "Charlie", 90000, "Engineering")]
df = spark.createDataFrame(data, ["id", "name", "salary", "dept"])

df.withColumn(
    "bonus",
    when((col("salary") > 70000) & (col("dept") == "Sales"), 5000)
    .when((col("salary") > 70000) & (col("dept") == "Engineering"), 7000)
    .otherwise(2000)
).show()
```

---

### **4. Nested Conditions**

```python
df.withColumn(
    "rating",
    when(col("salary") > 80000, 
         when(col("dept") == "Engineering", "A+").otherwise("A"))
    .when(col("salary") > 60000, "B")
    .otherwise("C")
).show()
```

---

### **5. Using with NULL checks**

```python
data = [(1, "Alice", 25), (2, "Bob", None), (3, None, 35)]
df = spark.createDataFrame(data, ["id", "name", "age"])

df.withColumn(
    "age_status",
    when(col("age").isNull(), "Unknown")
    .when(col("age") > 30, "Senior")
    .otherwise("Junior")
).show()
```

---

### **6. Replace Values Conditionally**

```python
# Update existing column
df.withColumn(
    "age",
    when(col("age").isNull(), 0).otherwise(col("age"))
).show()
```

